        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: William Shakespeare, Portia\n- Works: The Merchant of Venice\n- Places: Venice, Venetian Court of Justice\n- Concepts: The quality of mercy speech\n\nFacts:\n- William Shakespeare wrote The Merchant of Venice.\n- The Merchant of Venice is described in the chunk as a 16th-century opera play.\n- The Merchant of Venice is about a merchant in Venice who must default on a large loan from an abused Jewish moneylender.\n- Portia delivers the \"quality of mercy\" speech in William Shakespeare's The Merchant of Venice.\n- Portia's \"quality of mercy\" speech occurs in Act IV, Scene 1.\n- Act IV, Scene 1 is set in a Venetian Court of Justice.",
